{"name":"North Cape Grey","hex":"#7a9595","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"north","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The direction towards the pole to the left-hand side of someone facing east, specifically 0°, or (on another celestial object) the direction towards the pole lying on the northern side of the invariable plane.","The up or positive direction."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the north; northern.","Toward the north; northward."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north"},{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"North","blocks":[{"text":"North is one of the four compass points or cardinal directions. It is the opposite of south and is perpendicular to east and west. North is a noun, adjective, or adverb indicating direction or geography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Compass_Rose_English_North.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_North.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North"},{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a v